    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d955">

                <pb facs="0857" n="850" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg850"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.94244/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-22T00:00:00+09:00">January 22,
                        1937—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received January 22—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. My British colleague informs me that his Government is much upset at the
                    serious increase in smuggling in North China which developed during November and
                    December. He states that sugar and kerosene are the two items which show much
                    the largest increases and since both of these items seriously affect British
                    trade, he is instructed, unless he sees serious objection, again to draw the
                    attention of the Japanese Government to the matter. Before taking action,
                    however, he is directed to consult me and he did so this evening. He believes
                        <pb facs="0858" n="851" xml:id="pg851"/> that Lindsay<anchor n="68"
                        xml:id="d955-f1"/> has informed the Department and that I may receive
                    similar instructions.</p>
                <p>I have heard nothing about these new developments in China and I told Clive that
                    I could not act unless or until instructed.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d955-f1" n="68" xml:id="d955-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Ronald Lindsay, British Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
